.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DEVI_DEVICE_REMOVE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_devi_device_isremoved ,
.Nm ndi_devi_device_remove ,
.Nm ndi_devi_device_insert
.Nd record physical removal and reinsertion of a device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_device_isremoved
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_device_remove
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_device_insert
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Device node whose physical-presence state is accessed.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions maintain physical-presence state for hotplug devices that
cannot yet be detached, for example because an application has the device open.
They do not detach a driver or free a device node.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_device_remove()\fP marks the device physically removed and hidden,
updates device-event state, invalidates the device-information cache, and
posts removal notification.
Repeating the call on an already removed device has no effect.
\fBndi_devi_device_insert()\fP clears the removed and hidden state and posts
insertion notification when a removed device is reinserted.
Both operations require the caller to own the parent's critical section.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_device_isremoved()\fP tests the recorded removed state.
The caller must keep the node valid and serialize with state changes when a
consistent result is required.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user or kernel context.
They may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_devi_device_isremoved()\fP returns nonzero if the device is marked
removed, and zero otherwise.
The remove and insert functions return 1 when they change state and 0 when
the requested state was already recorded.
These are boolean results, not NDI status codes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_dev_is_prom_node 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_enter 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_online 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
